WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.270
Privacy and security begin with recognizing what the local AI system may store: prompts,

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.000
outputs, uploaded documents, conversation history, logs, model files, API keys,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.500
configuration, and backups.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.145
Any of these can contain sensitive information.

00:00:14.145 --> 00:00:18.170
Running on a Mac does not automatically make the workflow private if data is later synced,

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.500
logged, shared, or backed up without control.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.500
Cloud sync folders deserve caution.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.400
A model workspace, prompt archive, document collection,

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.500
or debug log stored in a synced folder may leave the local machine.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.000
Screenshots, exported conversations, and notebooks can also expose sensitive details.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.360
Decide what data is allowed in the local AI workflow, where it is stored,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.470
how long it is retained, and how it is deleted.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.500
Model files are supply chain artifacts.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.730
Prefer trusted sources, track provenance, and review licensing.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:47.500
Protect API keys and secrets used by local tools or remote endpoints.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.325
On shared Macs,

00:00:48.325 --> 00:00:52.495
user accounts and file permissions matter because another local user may access

00:00:52.495 --> 00:00:53.500
conversations,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.270
model caches, or configuration if storage is not separated appropriately.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.926
Operations include backups, update and rollback planning, and monitoring.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:03.500
Back up configuration and notes that are hard to recreate,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.470
but avoid preserving sensitive prompts forever by accident.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.000
Monitor disk usage, memory pressure, temperature, and service health.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
If a configuration breaks after an update,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.480
documented settings and a recovery path are more valuable than memory of what once worked.
